Hi Bill

An update:

> I believe the answer to the first is "yes".  For one thing, I think =
the LaTeX being submitted to arXiv (arxiv.org) is improving.  I commonly =
look at arXiv source and try to run it through tex4ht toward html+mathml =
with mathjax.  I see success there as a sign of well-structured LaTeX.  =
But I've not made a systematic investigation on this point.

But Bruce and Gabor have.  They have worked on the whole arXiv (to =
produce, in particular, very information-rich MathML) as part of the =
semantic maths project.  So they can probably give you lots of useful =
data on this and on many other subjects of interest to LATEX-L =
discussions.

Best,
chris



